    {
      "id": "fnfyphf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Features"
    },
    {
      "id": "3w0syr8",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Use of both stone and copper tools.",
        "Agriculture was well developed.",
        "Painted pottery was used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gwgztwx",
      "content": "Important SSC Point: Chalcolithic Age should not be confused with the Bronze Age. Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, while Chalcolithic tools used only copper."
    },
    {
      "id": "hhrukzi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Comparative Overview (Very Important for Exams)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Chalcolithic phase represents the first stage in human history where metal (copper) was used along with stone tools.",
        "Prominent regional cultures include Ahar-Banas culture (Rajasthan), Malwa culture (Madhya Pradesh), and Jorwe culture (Maharashtra).",
        "Wheel-made Black and Red Ware (BRW) decorated with white geometric patterns was the predominant pottery style.",
        "Agriculture and pastoralism formed the economic backbone, cultivating wheat, barley, rice, and lentils."
      ],
      "id": "i9i602p"
    },
